# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text Seven ships stand on the flat in the settling brown, three kilometres short of a glow. At midnight the board cleared one more command, lights only, nothing that moves, and {A} sent it. At two kilometres up the brown turned white from underneath: Cargo 2, spending its saved battery on every floodlight it had, and every pilot at a manual takeover had a mark to steer by, each blind in their own plume at the last. {B} set down closest. The glow is dimmer now, still there. The first crate out of Cargo 2's hold says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text {B}'s ship is the one the gust caught. It stands upright on the slope three kilometres from Cargo 2, a leg strut folded under it, and the first walk-round says what the readouts said: it will not fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung for a long minute, then starts a list of what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols later {A}, who wanted to answer from the start, climbs the rim with a second suit at the foot of it, counts the dark between flares, and answers from two hundred metres, inside the tick. HELLO RX · OK. To Starbase: "Landed. Seven down, six to fly. Found the eighth."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, night pass, half rations on seven galley tables. Below, the storm; on the night side, one lamp, steady since the handshake, blinking twice as the fleet passes over. Cargo 2's manifest comes up a line a pass, and tonight {A} reads: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Seven hungry people cheer a drill bit. The tile on {B}'s hinge line read hot on the way in; nobody says so tonight. A week later the storm clears. Seven entry streaks, one an orbit behind, waiting on a kinder angle. The tile holds. The first crate the rover brings back says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. The long orbit is over: by last night all seven ships were down on the flat. For two weeks a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and the strobe has been dark since midnight. {A} kneels at the service port with a battery pack and a radio, {B} a step behind in the second suit, counting aloud. Clip, latch, wait. Nine. Ten. Eleven. A click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand, from two metres, inside the tick. HELLO RX · OK. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Old Friend
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, thirty kilometres out, {A} driving, {B} watching the battery go past half while the steady light ahead gets no closer. The sums are plain: there and back is more than the rover has. {A} keeps driving. Two kilometres out, Cargo 2 hears the rover and runs the pad crew's arrival routine, written for a truck from the hangar: floods, strobe, hatch lamp, and a charge port on the landing leg, warm and waiting. {A} laughs out loud. {B} plugs the rover in, and they drive home slow on Cargo 2's sunlight. The first crate says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2, the rover parked nose to the strobe, {A} and {B} in the cab. On the first sol Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit; the spare is in that hold. The rover's spare batteries went into its heaters on the second night, when the cold came early; the last one is flat. {A} counts the dark: nine, ten, eleven, flare, and answers. HELLO RX · OK. The hold unlatches. Then Cargo 2 does what the pad patch says, wakes every survival heater at once with no battery check, and the strobe goes out for good. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth, in time."

